, Middle East, \u0026 Africa","description":"Europe, Middle East, \u0026 Africa","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#prodigy-education-eks-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"prodigy-education-eks-case-study","dateCreated":"2024-06-07T20:17:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-06-07T20:19:31+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Prodigy Education wanted to increase developer autonomy and enhance the reliability and scalability of its gamed-based learning offering. In 2019, the company migrated to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS), a managed Kubernetes service to run Kubernetes on Amazon Web Services (AWS). By migrating to Amazon EKS and using open-source tools, Prodigy Education boosted staff productivity, increased the reliability of its games, saved on compute costs, and improved scalability.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/prodigy%20logo%401x.ab730de66c6bc285a49546721043d76e632bd694.png","displayLocation":"Canada","customerNameLower":"prodigy","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Education","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/prodigy-education-eks-case-study/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","enableShare":"1","customer-name":"Prodigy","headline":"Saving Up to 60% on Compute Costs Using Amazon EKS and Karpenter with Prodigy Education","contentType":"Customer Story"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#education","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Education","description":"Education","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:01+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#public-sector","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Public Sector","description":"Public Sector","dateCreated":"2019-09-23T21:02:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:31